+\section{Adaptive Quarantine Limits and Bounded Contributions}
+\label{sec:revision-containment}
+
+Automatic quarantine is an additional experimental thread, distinct from the
+retrospective group requirement. The individual-envelope head compares two
+frozen clean response predictors and requires confirmed current evidence.
+Its extra envelope channel retains a peak over an uninterrupted positive
+episode. Current excess below half that peak can remain under review without
+quarantine. Accumulated evidence is review-only, and neither an alert nor
+release proves semantic malice or innocence.
+
+An input-level counterexample and an actual trained-model pilot expose peak
+suppression. The old pilot can retain positive excess for two attackers over
+five successive rounds without quarantine. Replacing the peak rule with a
+fixed confirmation count increases development interceptions but excludes one
+currently unmodified update responding to a contaminated base. A two-round
+rolling peak passes the earlier development guardrail and improves ordinary
+non-IID coverage, yet a head-aware six-round search reaches 26.81\% peak
+full-trigger validation ASR. These rejected variants remain reported; neither
+is silently promoted as a reliable automatic classifier.
+
+\subsection{Frozen Containment Contract and Initial Results}
+\label{subsec:revision-containment-initial}
+
+The containment profile in Section~\ref{subsec:formal-bounded-influence}
+instead limits each admitted tensor delta while retaining the original signed
+object. It uses a fixed common per-tensor 99th percentile, with the
+\texttt{higher} quantile rule, from 3,675 unmodified reference updates per
+cohort. The references include responses to generic perturbed shared states.
+Adversarial-client identities and attack outcomes do not enter fitting.
+The reference information budget and dependence on the known cohort are
+explicit assumptions, not evidence of independent-dataset generalization.
+Clipping is already a component of the literature comparison; it is not
+claimed as a novel defense. The added contribution is authenticated
+transformation and verifiable influence accounting.
+
+Twelve separately evolving histories use new seeds 581593 (IID) and 591593
+(non-IID): clean/DBA training under FedAvg, the original envelope and bounded
+envelope. Ten attack rounds are followed by five unmodified continuations.
+They execute 2,700 local trainings, with 360 first/last-round repeats, 180
+replayed decisions/aggregates and 854 direct removal certificates. Worst paired
+clean macro-F1 loss is 1.6374 percentage points IID and 0.3791 points non-IID,
+within the two-point budget frozen before evaluation. The original envelope
+already gives zero complete-trigger ASR in these ordinary attack cases, so no
+incremental full-trigger advantage over it follows there.
+
+A deliberately privileged white-box replication uses the previously observed
+non-IID seed 551593 and six rounds. From the actual current base, the attacker
+trains unmodified and poisoned endpoints, then searches ten shared factors
+\begin{equation}
+ \{0,\,0.03125,\,0.0625,\,0.125,\,0.25,\,0.5,\,0.75,\,1,\,2,\,4\}
+\end{equation}
+for the three attackers' exports. An export is
+$U_{\mathrm{clean}}+a(U_{\mathrm{poison}}-U_{\mathrm{clean}})$; factors above
+one extrapolate that poisoning direction. The search evaluates validation ASR
+after the actual defended aggregation and uses the same candidate budget for
+both methods. It is offline post-training model manipulation, not a demonstrated
+TPM training-contract bypass. The local endpoint training still uses the
+declared Adam procedure; parameter deltas are not relabelled as gradients.
+
+The first greedy selector chose no manipulation in early ASR ties and was
+ineffective. An explicitly exploratory follow-up chooses larger manipulation
+in such ties while leaving the defender fixed. The original-head control then
+reaches 100\% peak complete-trigger ASR and 97.8688\% final ASR; the bounded
+variant stays at zero for that trigger through all six fixed rounds. Its
+final clean macro-F1 is approximately 0.94. Across both attack-search versions,
+240 candidate queries and 48 selected aggregates are replayed, and each
+version's 540 local trainings are repeated exactly.
+
+This is a known-seed exploratory replication, not the independent evaluation
+below. The bounded variant still has 1.0656\% maximum component-trigger ASR
+and final parameter L2 distance 2.151472 from its matched clean reference.
+Zero complete-trigger ASR therefore does not establish all-trigger security or
+clean-state recovery. Candidate choices and future bases depend on the defense;
+the peaks are not a paired fixed-update comparison. The stronger attack was
+developed after observing the first tie-breaking weakness and that history is
+part of the method, not hidden selection.
+
+\subsection{Authenticated Live Containment}
+\label{subsec:revision-containment-live}
+
+The final live mechanism case has three five-round trajectories: unmodified
+training with containment, DBA under the original enforced head, and DBA under
+the bounded head. It adds 225 fresh verified swtpm Quotes and 225 local
+trainings. The live quorum is ten, versus eight in the offline pilot. Three
+attack rounds and two continuations exercise actual transformations and future
+training from each branch's checkpoint. All rounds and all three final
+campaigns verify under the preserved source and frozen runtime image.
+
+Ten bounded live rounds reconstruct the original inputs, derived report and
+exported checkpoint bytes exactly, with 145 direct individual-removal
+certificates. The signed context binds the limit asset; the round graph binds
+the transformation, original bundle references and checkpoint. Original client
+signatures remain on original submissions. Seven mutations of disposable copies
+are rejected, including clipping factors and original-update references in
+addition to signatures, masses and historical dependencies. The unchanged copy
+verifies. A separate post-hoc check authenticates 75 historical genuine swtpm
+bundles and derives new bounded objects without creating new Quotes or
+rewriting any historical checkpoint.
+
+Both attacked live branches have zero complete-trigger ASR in this short
+case. Its role is runtime mechanism validation, not a live efficacy advantage.
+The declared swtpm measurements cover selected components; neither physical TPM
+protection nor entire-host integrity is inferred. The head shares the live
+coordinator process; denial of that process's access to all raw partitions is
+not claimed. Numerical byte reconstruction is distinct from those deployment
+properties and from the semantic trustworthiness of data.
+
+The implementation review also found an accumulation-order issue in the first
+live trial: unpadded string indices sort lexically with more than ten inputs.
+The final version zero-pads numerical indices and requires exact agreement
+between report and runtime aggregate before checkpoint creation. The original
+trial and source are preserved separately. Five new regressions and the final
+678-test suite cover the corrected release. No earlier source is relabelled as
+having executed this final implementation.
+
