+\end{table}
+
+Full WeiDetect evaluates fifteen local models on 2,238 auxiliary windows; full
+composite evaluates the base and local models on 3,223 validation windows and
+includes indicator construction, policy and aggregation. The envelope benchmark
+has 540 state-advancing operations, rather than idempotent retries. Actual-gradient
+server recurrences have medians 0.580/5.313/4.333 ms for FedAvg/literal Eq.~(2)/
+literal Eq.~(3); representative fifteen-client gradient collection has median
+38.736 ms. These dependent measurements do not imply confidence intervals or
+production latency guarantees.
+
+\subsection{Retrospective Candidate Groups and Controlled Removal}
+\label{subsec:revision-retrospective-groups}
+
+The agreed group analysis is retrospective and distinct from automatic
+quarantine. The V2 selector uses median-centered update similarity, tensor
+profiles and temporal indicator associations. Each cohort has three clean
+fitting histories and three disjoint clean threshold histories, using only
+rounds 1--10. Candidate selection closes before evaluation identities, ASR and
+rounds 11--15 are read. Evaluation is a secondary analysis of twelve existing
+shadow-FedAvg histories, not untouched prospective group discovery.
+
+V2 ranks maximal cliques by their weakest conditioned edge and selects the
+first retaining eight contributors. In all six attacked evaluation cases, the
+priority pair contains two true members, no false member and one missed attacker.
+Across the wider candidate pools there are 15 true and 16 false members, with
+three attackers absent from the pools. Six clean histories return no group.
+The comparison envelope prefix set contains all three scripted attackers in
+each attacked case, but exact experimental membership is not evidence of
+pairwise cooperation or intent. Different reference budgets further limit
+direct ranking of the two selectors.
+
+Each selected set is removed individually and jointly at round 10. Survivors
+retain their original decisions and weights are renormalized. The 293 direct
+outputs are reconstructed. Up to twenty hash-random benign subsets of equal
+size, plus the benign subset closest in original sample mass, provide controls
+chosen before effects are inspected. Equal client counts can remove different
+mass, particularly under non-IID data. A joint improvement beyond individual
+removal is a descriptive contrast, not a p-value or a proof of collusion.
+
+For the hard non-IID seed 512593, source round-10 ASR is 97.59\%. Removing the
+three-member envelope set jointly lowers it to 49.30\%, whereas the two-member
+V2 group yields 93.33\%. Other source cases already have near-zero or zero ASR
+and supply little evidence of reduction. Each intervention therefore retains
+its source rate, individual removals and benign controls.
+
+Selected memberships are then held fixed while successors really train from
+the corrected branch base. Five later rounds are not reconstructed by reusing
+updates trained on the original checkpoint. The same-start comparison uses
+experimental $W_9$, with a separate unmodified training reference of identical
+participation. Equality from that point alone cannot certify a clean earlier
+history. Late removal of all three selected attackers in the hard case leaves
+1.68\% validation ASR and 1.54\% test ASR at round 15.
+
+\begin{table}[tbp]
+\centering\small
+\caption[Late correction and complete rewind]{Hard-case round-15 test results.
+The reduced-population rewind and its reference exclude the same selected set throughout.}
+\label{tab:revision-rewind}
+\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{Xrr}
+\toprule
+Intervention & ASR (\%) & Macro-F1 (\%) \\
+\midrule
+Original all-client scripted attack & 99.91 & 94.45 \\
+Late selected-set removal at round 10 & 1.54 & 95.98 \\
+Replay from $W_0$, selected set excluded & 0.00 & 95.96 \\
+Matched unmodified reference, same exclusions & 0.00 & 95.96 \\
+Privileged unmodified replay, all clients & 0.00 & 94.50 \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabularx}
+\end{table}
+
+The separate complete rewind excludes the unchanged selected set from rounds
+1--15 and matches every checkpoint of its reduced-population unmodified
+reference. A privileged all-client unmodified replay matches the original
+all-client clean history, but needs correct snapshots, starting model, seeds,
+optimizer and deterministic runtime. A snapshot commitment alone does not
+establish semantic cleanliness. The two interventions concern different
+populations and must not be conflated. Neither rewrites the historical record
+or establishes certified unlearning in an arbitrary deployment.
+
+The group continuation and rewind studies execute 5,670 local trainings in
+their declared phases. The existing test fold is evaluated at fixed endpoints;
+it has been used by earlier studies and is not a pristine external holdout.
+The conclusion is limited to groups \emph{compatible with coordinated behavior}
+under the stated evidence and controls. False candidates and missed members
+remain part of the result.
