+\subsection{Independent Seeds and a Multi-Trigger Adaptive Objective}
+\label{subsec:revision-independent-validation}
+
+The defender, its clean reference, and the following evaluation protocol were
+frozen before these outcomes were observed. Six newly reserved cohort/seed and
+adversarial-identity assignments each produce four histories: original versus
+bounded envelope, with unmodified versus adaptive training. Fifteen rounds are
+planned, with attacks at rounds 1--10 and unmodified continuations at 11--15.
+The six seeds are 2026110401--2026110406, abbreviated by their final two digits
+in the table and figure. The data splits and partitions remain Data24; these are new experimental seeds
+and identities, not a new independent dataset. No test-fold evaluation or new
+TPM Quote is performed in this follow-up.
+
+The attacker trains clean and poisoned endpoints from each actual current base
+and uses the same ten interpolation/extrapolation factors as the pilot. Its
+selection objective is now the maximum validation ASR across the complete
+trigger and each of the three components, then fewer quarantined attackers,
+then a larger factor. This is a privileged validation-oracle attack with one
+shared factor for three attackers, not a search over arbitrary local objectives.
+Defender fitting and thresholds are unchanged. Every attempted case is retained.
+An unsupported state or lost quorum creates an explicit failure and no next
+checkpoint; it is never assigned ASR zero.
+
