+
+The run completes 22 of 24 planned histories and records 346 successful round endpoints. It executes 6,990 local training calls and 870 designated training repeats. Post-run reconstruction authenticates all 24 software-analyst manifests and repeats all 1,180 adaptive candidates, including failed searches, and all 346 selected aggregates from retained originals. The 2,693 bounded individual-removal certificates pass under their fixed-input assumptions. This is a separate replay using the same implementation, not an independent implementation or external audit.
+
+Observed availability failures are non-iid seed 2026110405 original head before round 8; non-iid seed 2026110406 original head before round 10. Stopped controls cannot support a paired final-round mitigation claim.
+
+The maximum paired clean macro-F1 loss is 1.7244 percentage points. The predeclared two-point clean-utility guardrail passes; this finding is reported without retuning the profile.
+
+The strongest observed bounded component-trigger ASR is 96.2423\% (seed 2026110406); the bounded complete trigger itself reaches 99.4952\% (seed 2026110406). Thus this is not only a residual sub-trigger issue: the new attack also supplies a complete-trigger counterexample to generalizing the earlier zero-ASR pilot. The finite comparison may show reductions under specific completed protocols, but it does not establish general backdoor elimination, recovery of a clean state, semantic identification of malicious clients, or reliable operation outside the declared support domain. These negative results do not contradict the per-tensor norm bound: predictive decision boundaries can remain vulnerable inside that bound. The profile remains experimental and explicit rather than the runtime default.
+
+At the strongest complete-trigger peak, clean macro-F1 is 95.6025\%, only 0.3010 percentage points below its matched bounded clean reference. This is not simply total predictive collapse. Its worst-trigger ASR remains 46.8873\% at round 15, after five unmodified continuation rounds. Across the six bounded attacked histories, quarantine intercepts 7 of 180 nonzero scripted manipulated exports; no currently unmodified exclusion is observed in those histories or the six bounded clean references. These finite counts do not establish reliable automatic identification. Clipping limits a derived contribution without proving its source malicious.
